        "title": "Example Cryogenic Tank Insulation Test Results",
        "abstract": "Multilayer insulation for an example liquid hydrogen tank was tested in a vacuum chamber at three boundary temperatures. Heat leak, boil-off and pressure rise were measured over 30 days. The measured heat leak was 12 percent below the model's prediction at the warm boundary and 4 percent above it at the cold boundary. This memorandum gives the test set-up, the instrumentation, the data and a comparison with two thermal models used in design.",
